===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|gases}} The gases surrounding the [[Earth]] or any [[astronomical]] body.
#: {{meronyms|en|Thesaurus:atmosphere}}
#: {{cot|en|hydrosphere|biosphere}}
# {{senseid|en|air}} The [[air]] in a [[particular]] place.
#* {{RQ:Landon Francesca Carrara|page=2|volume=I|text=The last hue of crimson had died away in the west, and the depth of the rich purple '''atmosphere''' was unbroken.}}
#* {{RQ:Belloc Lowndes Lodger|I|0016
|passage=Thus the red damask curtains which now shut out the fog-laden, drizzling '''atmosphere''' of the Marylebone Road, had cost a mere song, and yet they might have been warranted to last another thirty years. A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the floor;{{nb...}}.}}
# {{senseid|en|conditions}} {{label|en|figuratively}} The conditions (such as music, illumination etc.) that can influence the [[mood]] felt in an [[environment]].
#: {{syn|en|air|ambiance}}
# {{senseid|en|mood}} {{label|en|figuratively}} The apparent [[mood]] felt in an [[environment]].
#: {{syn|en|feeling|mood}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XX|33|For by the hearth the children sit<br>⁠Cold in that '''atmosphere''' of Death,<br>⁠And scarce endure to draw the breath,<br>Or like to noiseless phantoms flit: […]}}
#* {{quote-song|1=en|year=1984|artist=w:Russ Abbot|author=Ben Findon; Eddie Tucker; {{w|Steve Rodway}}|title=Atmosphere|album=I Love a Party|text=Oh, what an '''atmosphere''' / I love a party with a happy '''atmosphere'''}}
# {{senseid|en|unit}} A unit of measurement for pressure equal to 101325 Pa (symbol: {{l|mul|atm}}), approximately the [[atmospheric pressure]] at [[sea level]].
# {{senseid|en|extras}} {{lb|en|television|film|uncountable}} [[extra|Extras]] in a [[scene]] who have no spoken lines.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2006|journal=Los Angeles Magazine|volume=51|issue=2|page=100
|passage=Central Casting is in the business of extras, also known as '''atmosphere''' or background actors {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Kerry Segrave|title=Extras of Early Hollywood: A History of the Crowd, 1913-1945|page=38
|passage="It is estimated conservatively that there are some 50,000 would-be film extras in and around the celluloid capital, persons who would jump at the opportunity to appear as '''atmosphere''' in pictures," Scott concluded.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=William R. Phillippe|title=The Pastor's Diary
|passage=By the way, I discovered that we were not extras but background, as far as the director was concerned; and for the producer, we were '''atmosphere'''.}}

